 "_": "Wrist camera bracket: an L reaching from the flange disc's rear face out past the fork cheeks, holding a 16 square board camera looking DOWN the tool's −Z. It is on the blade, so J5 aims it and the hand-eye transform is a constant. It cannot see the grip point — nothing on the wrist can, with a Ø104 tool in front of it — and it does not pretend to: this is the camera that finds the can on the bench, not the one that watches the jaws close. One extrude along +Z, one pocket.",
